<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Runtime - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/runtime/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/runtime/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go: GPM Quantity Limits</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/go_gpm_quantity_limit/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 Dec 2024 14:16:42 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/go_gpm_quantity_limit/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/techarticle/">TechArticle</category><description>Detailed explanation of the quantity limits in Go's GPM model.</description></item><item><title>An Overview of Go GC (Garbage Collection)</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/a_brief_discussion_on_go_gc_garbage_collection/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Dec 2024 13:03:08 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/a_brief_discussion_on_go_gc_garbage_collection/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/techarticle/">TechArticle</category><description>Detailed explanation of the principles and implementation of Go's garbage collection mechanism.</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 097</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_097/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:25 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_097/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var p *int&#10;&#10;func foo() (*int, error) {&#10; var i int = 5&#10; return &amp;amp;i, nil&#10;}&#10;&#10;func bar() {&#10; //use p&#10; fmt.Println(*p)&#10;}&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; p, err := foo()&#10; if err != nil {&#10; fmt.Println(err)&#10; return&#10; }&#10; bar()&#10; fmt.Println(*p)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. 5 5&#10;B. runtime error&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;B&#10;The global &lt;code&gt;*p&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt;.&#10;In &lt;code&gt;p, err := foo()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt; here is a new local variable and is unrelated to the global &lt;code&gt;p&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>